<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#nayaka">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nayaka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nayak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nayaka, meaning leader or chief, was a title for military commanders in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-india">South India</a>. Under the Kakatiya dynasty and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, Nayakas held land and revenues in return for providing troops, and many later became hereditary rulers. After Vijayanagara declined, Nayaka dynasties governed kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gingee">Gingee</a>.</p></div>
